-- title:
--   Theorem 3.1 — SPeL1 with θρ ≤ 1: {x^k} is bounded, its cluster points are feasible, and a cluster point satisfying (3.14) is a stationary point of (1.4)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $A\in\mathbb R^{m\times n}$, $b\in\mathbb R^m$, and the blanket assumptions of the paper (p. 1) hold for $q=1$: $\sigma\ge 0$, $\mathrm{FEA}(A,b,\sigma,1)=\{x:\|Ax-b\|_1\le\sigma\}\neq\emptyset$ and $\|b\|_1>\sigma$. Let $0<p<1$ and $\Phi(x)=\|x\|_p^p$.
--
--   Let $\{x^k\}_{k\ge0}$ be a sequence generated by the smoothing penalty method SPeL1 (Algorithm 1, p. 14) from a feasible $x^{\mathrm{feas}}$ and parameters $\lambda_0,\mu_0,\nu_0,\epsilon_0>0$, $\rho>1$, $0<\theta<1$ with
--   $$\theta\rho\le1 .$$
--   The inner method of Step 2 is arbitrary, subject only to (3.8)–(3.10). Then:
--
--   1. $\{x^k\}$ is bounded;
--   2. every cluster point $x^*$ of $\{x^k\}$ is a feasible point of (1.4), $\|Ax^*-b\|_1\le\sigma$;
--   3. if $x^*$ is a cluster point of $\{x^k\}$ at which
--   $$-\partial^\infty\Phi(x^*)\cap\mathcal N_{\mathrm{FEA}(A,b,\sigma,1)}(x^*)=\{0\}, \tag{3.14}$$
--   then $x^*$ is a stationary point of (1.4): $x^*\in\mathrm{FEA}(A,b,\sigma,1)$ and $0\in\partial(\Phi+\delta_{\mathrm{FEA}(A,b,\sigma,1)})(x^*)$.
--
--   Here $\partial$ and $\partial^\infty$ are the limiting and horizon subdifferentials and $\mathcal N$ the normal cone. The theorem is the convergence guarantee of the paper's algorithm: although finding a global minimizer of (1.4) is NP-hard, every cluster point of SPeL1 is feasible and, under the constraint qualification (3.14), stationary.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Algorithm 1 is a predicate on an infinite sequence (the theorem concerns $\{x^k\}_{k=0}^\infty$), with the inner points $x^{k,l_k}$ and $x^{k,l_k+1}$ existentially quantified and the parameter updates of Step 3 in closed form. The gradient $\nabla f_{\lambda,\mu,\nu}$ is the paper's formula (3.11)–(3.13). Subdifferentials are taken in Euclidean space; a cluster point is a `MapClusterPt` of the sequence.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: the while loop of Algorithm 1 with parameter updates λ_{k+1} = ρλ_k, μ_{k+1} = θμ_k, ν_{k+1} = θν_k, ϵ_{k+1} = θϵ_k → predicate IsSPeL1 on x : ℕ → ℝⁿ with λ_k = ρ^kλ₀, μ_k = θ^kμ₀, ν_k = θ^kν₀, ϵ_k = θ^kϵ₀ and inner points z k = x^{k,l_k}, w k = x^{k,l_k+1} existentially quantified; reason: the theorem is about the infinite sequence {x^k}; the closed forms solve the Step 3 recursion
--   - encoding: (3.8) dist(0, ∂Φ(x^{k,l_k+1}) + ∇f(x^{k,l_k})) ≤ ϵ_k → ∃ ξ ∈ ∂Φ(w k), ‖ξ + ∇f(z k)‖₂ ≤ ϵ_k; reason: the limiting subdifferential is closed, so the distance is attained when ∂Φ(w) ≠ ∅, and dist to ∅ is +∞
--   - encoding: ∇f_{λ,μ,ν} → the explicit formula (3.11)–(3.13) (gradFSm); reason: the paper's own expression for the gradient
--   - encoding: λ_k ↓ 0 in the definition of ∂^∞ (p. 3); 𝒩_FEA; cluster point → λ_k > 0 and λ_k → 0; limiting subdifferential of the indicator of FEA(A,b,σ,1); MapClusterPt; reason: a positive null sequence has a decreasing subsequence along which the other limits persist; 𝒩 = ∂δ as in [33]; same notions
-- source:
--   Yang, Chen & Xiang, Sparse solutions of a class of constrained optimization problems, arXiv:1907.00880v5, p. 14, Theorem 3.1 (Algorithm 1 p. 14; Definition 3.1 p. 12; subdifferentials p. 3); proof pp. 15–17

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SparseLpLq_SmallP_Setting
import Definitions.Def_SparseLpLq_SmallP_Supplement_Variational
import Definitions.Def_SparseLpLq_SmallP_Supplement_SPeL1

open scoped ENNReal Matrix Topology

namespace SparseLpLq.SmallP.Supplement
open SparseLpLq.SmallP
theorem theorem_3_1 {m n : ℕ} (A : Matrix (Fin m) (Fin n) ℝ) (b : Fin m → ℝ) (σ : ℝ)
    (hσ : 0 ≤ σ) (hfeas : (FEA A b σ 1).Nonempty) (hb : σ < qNorm 1 b)
    (p : ℝ) (hp : p ∈ Set.Ioo (0 : ℝ) 1)
    (xfeas : Fin n → ℝ) (lam0 μ0 ν0 ε0 ρ θ : ℝ) (hθρ : θ * ρ ≤ 1)
    (x : ℕ → Fin n → ℝ) (hx : IsSPeL1 A b σ p xfeas lam0 μ0 ν0 ε0 ρ θ x) :
    -- (i)
    Bornology.IsBounded (Set.range x) ∧
    -- (ii)
    (∀ xs : Fin n → ℝ, MapClusterPt xs Filter.atTop x → xs ∈ FEA A b σ 1) ∧
    -- (iii)
    (∀ xs : Fin n → ℝ, MapClusterPt xs Filter.atTop x →
      {d | -d ∈ horizonSubdiff (PhiE p) (WithLp.toLp 2 xs)} ∩ normalConeFEA A b σ xs = {0} →
      IsStationary A b σ p xs) := by sorry
end SparseLpLq.SmallP.Supplement
